    "title": "Samuel Hernandez's team, the Peoria Chiefs, fall 6-5 to Lansing Lugnuts on Tuesday, Aug. 18",
    "text": "Samuel Hernandez’s team, the Peoria Chiefs, fall 6-5 to Lansing Lugnuts on Tuesday, Aug. 18\nOn Tuesday, Aug. 18, at 7:05 p.m., the Peoria Chiefs, the current team of former Lakeland High School standout Samuel Hernandez, fell 6-5 to the Lansing Lugnuts in a MiLB game.\nThe game was played at Jackson Field. It was the first meeting between the teams this season.\nHernandez was 0-for-4, drew 1 walk, struck out twice and left 2 runners on base.\nThe Chiefs are scheduled to play the Lugnuts again at Jackson Field on Wednesday, Aug. 19.\nSamuel Hernandez — Catcher — 5′9″ — 185 — Hometown: Oklahoma City",
    "summary": "Samuel Hernandez’s team, the Peoria Chiefs, fall 6-5 to Lansing Lugnuts on Tuesday, Aug. 18 On Tuesday, Aug. 18, at 7:05 p.m., the Peoria Chiefs, the current team of former Lakeland High School standout Samuel Hernandez, fell 6-5 to the Lansing Lugnuts in a MiLB game. The game was played at Jackson Field. Hernandez was 0-for-4, drew 1 walk, struck out twice and left 2 runners on base. The Chiefs are scheduled to play the Lugnuts again at Jackson Field on Wednesday, Aug. 19. Samuel Hernandez — Catcher — 5′9″ — 185 — Hometown: Oklahoma City",
